1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:07,708
In nineteen fifty, Erwin Chargaff analysed DNA from many species and found a strange regularity.

2
00:00:07,708 --> 00:00:13,606
Adenine always equals thymine, and guanine always equals cytosine.

3
00:00:13,606 --> 00:00:16,445
So purines equal pyrimidines.

4
00:00:16,445 --> 00:00:22,252
Only the ratio of A plus T to G plus C changes from species to species.

